# Issue #26-MED-009 — codified review ownership.
#
# CODEOWNERS turns the implicit "ask the maintainer" review pattern
# into an enforced GitHub Branch Protection rule. Any PR touching a
# path below auto-requests review from the listed owner(s); branch
# protection rejects merges without that approval.
#
# All paths default to the @Willen-Federation maintainer set. As the
# project grows, narrow paths to specific owners (e.g. iOS engineers
# for ios/**, backend reviewer for any future server-shared schema).
#
# Format: <path>  <owner1> [owner2] ...
# Owners can be @org/team or @username. See:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Catch-all — every PR requests review from the maintainer set.
*                                @Willen-Federation/maintainers

# Native + entitlement files are particularly sensitive. Keep an
# explicit second owner / native engineer reviewer here once a
# native-only sub-team exists.
/android/**                      @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/ios/**                          @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements  @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml  @Willen-Federation/maintainers

# CI / workflow changes touch the supply chain — extra eyes.
/.github/                        @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/.github/workflows/              @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/.github/dependabot.yml          @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS              @Willen-Federation/maintainers

# Auth & security surfaces — always require maintainer review.
/lib/core/auth/                  @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/lib/core/network/url_validator.dart       @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/lib/core/network/pinned_http_client.dart  @Willen-Federation/maintainers
/lib/core/storage/secure_storage.dart      @Willen-Federation/maintainers
